    "user_request_original": "Perform one bounded TMM thickness optimization for an exactly 14-layer planar stack. Use the fixed material sequence from the incident side: HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2. Optimize only the physical thickness of each finite layer within the user-declared bounds. Do not optimize material identity or layer count in this route. Optimize a 14-layer HfO2/SiO2 alternating stack on fused silica substrate with air incident medium. Initialize thicknesses from round 1 best candidate: [50.69, 81.96, 44.76, 74.71, 61.68, 82.14, 65.10, 121.47, 70.87, 91.78, 79.48, 119.16, 63.56, 64.70] nm. Apply ±6nm absolute bounds on each layer thickness. Use gradient-based optimizer (L-BFGS or BFGS variant) with learning rate 0.025. Evaluate transmittance at 1530-1565nm band and reflectance at 400-700nm band at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Total layers fixed at 14. Material sequence: HfO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1530-1565 nm, 400-700 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 1530-1565 nm band; High reflectance in 400-700 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Low reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band; Low transmittance in 400-700 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Maximum 30 layers.",
